PocketSlicer is built on libslic3r and the printer profiles of OrcaSlicer
(https://github.com/SoftFever/OrcaSlicer), which derives from Bambu Studio
(Bambu Lab), PrusaSlicer (Prusa Research) and Slic3r (Alessandro Ranellucci and
contributors). All of them are licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0. OrcaSlicer is
included as the git submodule third_party/OrcaSlicer, with the changes in
native/patches.

The APK also contains printer, process and filament profiles copied from Bambu
Studio (Bambu Lab), Creality Print (Creality), QIDI Studio (QIDI) and Snapmaker
Orca (Snapmaker), all licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0; see profiles/imported.

The APK contains the following third-party software. Versions are those pinned by
OrcaSlicer v2.4.2 (third_party/OrcaSlicer/deps), except OpenSSL, set in native/deps; the full license
texts are in each project's source distribution.

